      "text": "War history from the annals of the US Army 11th Airborne Division in the Philippines. I have had lunch and dinner at the Manila Polo Club often as a guest- right next to the polo field mentioned in the article, and had no idea of any of the war history there from the Battle of Manila. It's right in the heart of Forbes Park, the wealthiest suburb in the nation. Preserving our shared war 🇺🇸🇵🇭🇯🇵 history together is important in my opinion.  I wonder if there will be another fire fight on the polo field only this time leaving the field littered with dead PLA troops instead? It would be nice to avoid that, but it seems like China didn't learn the same lessons from WW2 that the rest of us learned, so we might end up repeating history there",
